# Files that must never be uploaded to a deployment.
#
# `vercel deploy` from the CLI uploads the working directory, not the git index,
# so anything sitting untracked next to the source goes up with it. This repo
# accumulates raw video masters (tens of MB each) and vendored skill/agent
# directories that have nothing to do with the build. They inflate every upload,
# count against the deployment size limit, and — for the source footage — would
# be publicly reachable if they ever landed under `public/`.
#
# Deployments driven by the Git integration only ever see committed files, so
# this is belt-and-braces there. It is load-bearing for CLI deploys.

# ── Raw video masters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The shipped, compressed cut lives at `public/hero.mp4`. These are the sources
# it was cut from, and they sit in the repo root.
#
# Anchored to the root with a leading slash rather than written as `*.mp4` with
# a `!public/hero.mp4` exception: if the negation were ever mis-evaluated the
# site would deploy with no hero film at all, and this pattern cannot reach
# inside `public/` to begin with.
/*.mp4

# ── Tooling that is not part of the app ───────────────────────────────────
.agents/
skills/
liquid-glass-skill/
.skills_repo_temp/
.claude/

# ── Test output and local artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
coverage/
tests/

# ── Docs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
